# The compiled circuit artifacts under code/circuits/*/target/ are committed
# (see code/.gitignore) because Vercel has no Noir toolchain. They are build
# output reproduced by `nargo compile` on Linux, so keep them byte-exact:
# without this, checking out on Windows rewrites LF to CRLF and every artifact
# shows up as modified against a freshly compiled one, hiding real drift in
# noise. `-text` disables end-of-line conversion in both directions.
code/circuits/*/target/*.json -text
code/circuits/*/target/kurier_vk_hash -text
